-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Decision functions answer `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "where", "if", "unless", "upon", "after" or "on" not
--                met, a period fixed in the text's own words and missed).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer (a scope limit, a lifted bar that grants nothing, a bare "must" not done).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer (the Court may order otherwise in the interests of justice).
-- The Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act and its Third Schedule are not among the sources: their facts are inputs.
-- PERIODS are counted under O 3 r 3 (lines 323 to 329): a "clear day" period excludes both its end days (r 3(5)); the last
-- day is the seam input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.

